          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "লাড্ডু (lāḍḍu) matches Sanskrit laḍḍu, \"a kind of sweetmeat\"; the Bengali word inherited from it is lāṛu, which CDIAL lists (CDIAL 10926). CDIAL takes the Sanskrit word as probably the same as laḍḍu, \"lump\", and notes a proposed link with Munda words for \"lump\"."
            }
          ]
        },
