            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গুড় (guṛ) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from guḍa, \"boiled sugarcane juice, molasses\" (CDIAL 4182). CDIAL lists Bengali guṛ, \"molasses\", and asks whether the word is the same as guḍa, \"ball\"."
